{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"c5188f993f3252da322e811e82e58f6346c6556f70853ba9a681c525254d6fde","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar_reconciler apply layer — comment dedup","key_entities":["BindingStore.is_comment_mapped","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_comment_dedup_seam_crossing.py","rebar_reconciler.outbound_comments._diff_comments","dispatch_apply_phases._record_comment_id","acli_cli_ops.add_comment","acli_subprocess._run_acli","ACLI_SUCCESS_ENVELOPE"],"problem_keywords":["dedup","seam-crossing","binding store","comment mapping","end-to-end test"],"propositions":["A unified seam-crossing test needed to verify dedup logic end-to-end, because prior unit tests seeded invariants independently (differ tests used _StubBindingStore, apply tests used synthetic payloads) and could not detect when is_comment_mapped guard was disabled.","The new test posts a real envelope through the real recording path (_record_comment_id against a real BindingStore), then re-diffs the same store with _diff_comments and asserts the recorded comment is skipped while an unrecorded control comment is still emitted.","An inert-guard variant monkeypatches is_comment_mapped to always return False and asserts the recorded comment is re-emitted, proving the skip depends on the guard rather than passing vacuously."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787713923112992001,"uuid":"cfe341c7-5cf2-4b8c-88eb-4bc070c54d54"}